> This document provides the detailed project plan for **Project Athena**, a strategic initiative to develop and launch NexaTech’s next-generation autonomous analytics agent. This project is a cornerstone of our 2026-2028 strategic plan and is critical to solidifying our leadership in AI-powered business intelligence.

## 1. Project Overview

### 1.1. Project Goal

The goal of Project Athena is to design, build, and launch an AI-powered agent that can autonomously analyze datasets, identify significant patterns and anomalies, generate narrative insights in natural language, and proactively provide recommendations to business users. This will fundamentally change how our customers interact with data, moving from a reactive, query-based model to a proactive, conversational, and insight-driven experience.

### 1.2. Scope

*   **In Scope:**
    *   Development of the core AI/ML models for data analysis and insight generation.
    *   Creation of a natural language generation (NLG) engine to produce narrative summaries.
    *   Integration of the Athena agent into the NexaInsight Platform.
    *   Design of a new conversational user interface (UI).
    *   Beta program with a select group of customers.
    *   General Availability (GA) launch.
*   **Out of Scope:**
    *   Integration with products other than the NexaInsight Platform in the initial release.
    *   Support for on-premise deployments in the initial release.

### 1.3. Success Metrics

*   **Adoption:** 25% of enterprise customers actively using Athena within 6 months of GA.
*   **Engagement:** 50% reduction in time-to-insight for common analytical tasks.
*   **Revenue:** Generate $5 million in new ARR attributable to Athena in the first year post-launch.
*   **Timeline:** Beta launch by September 30, 2026; GA by March 31, 2027.

